# The wrapper looks this one up as a *client*, and HIDL resolves the context of
# that lookup by the version-less package name - the same form android.hidl.*,
# android.hardware.* use in the platform's own hwservice_contexts.  Without this
# line it falls back to default_android_hwservice, which no domain may find, so
# IServiceManager::getService() returns null and the wrapper dies in its
# constructor (see the audit line: interface=vendor.oplus.hardware.biometrics.
# fingerprint::IBiometricsFingerprint).  The find itself is already granted by
# the hal_fingerprint_hwservice rule in hal_fingerprint_default.te.
